    "font" : "MLMRoman12-Regular",
    "font size" : 11.955,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "2.1. Permutations and compositions. Throughout the paper, let n be a nonnegative integer. The symmetric group Sn is the group of all permutations of the set [n] = {1,2,...,n}. We write permutations in one-line notation σ = [σ1,σ2,...,σn], with brackets to distinguish them from compositions. Given two permutations σ,π ∈ Sn, their product is the permutation σπ ∈ Sn defined by (σπ)i = σπ"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 18,
    "level" : "3",
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 71.283, 124.553, 540.005, 198.105 ],
    "font" : "MLMRoman12-Regular",
    "font size" : 11.955,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : ". The reverse rev(σ) of a permutation σ ∈ Sn is the permutation σw0 = [σn,σn−1,...,σ1], where w0 = [n,n − 1,···,1]. The symmetric group Sn is generated by the simple transpositions s1,s2,...,sn−1, where si swaps i and i + 1. The length ℓ(σ) of a permutation σ ∈ Sn is the smallest number of simple transpositions whose product equals σ. A reduced expression of a permutation σ is a sequence si"
  }, {
